<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <Description>Importers for embedded vector graphics: WMF, EMF, EMF+ and SVG, decoded into the Paperless display list.</Description>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!--
      SVG parsing and scene building. Deliberately NOT Svg.Skia: taking these three
      without it avoids pulling in a second SkiaSharp version, and keeps the output a
      device-independent command list we can translate into IDrawingSink rather than
      pixels. See the note in Directory.Packages.props.
    -->
    <PackageReference Include="Svg.SceneGraph" />
    <PackageReference Include="Svg.Model" />
    <PackageReference Include="ShimSkiaSharp" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!--
      The rectangle-set algebra under the clip is internal because nothing outside this library
      should be combining regions, but its correctness is the kind a test through a whole
      metafile cannot attribute: a band coalesced one row too far shows up as a picture drawn
      slightly too wide, which reads as a mapping bug.
    -->
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Paperless.Vector.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Paperless.Core\Paperless.Core.csproj" />
    <!--
      SVG text is resolved and shaped by Paperless.Text rather than by the SVG library's own
      font path, so a wordmark inside a picture and the paragraph beside it agree about what
      a family name means. No consumer gains a dependency by this: every reader already
      references Paperless.Text, and Paperless.Rendering does the same for the same reason.
    -->
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Paperless.Text\Paperless.Text.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
